  "limitations": [
    "All three lanes bind engine source 26fa28d0e7834515508fc07ac503164a6effc820 and published model version 3 81f924d4: RTX 5090 beta.4 and native RTX 3090/4090 v0.8.0 beta.1. Runtime eligibility does not grant candidate-bound external-install acceptance, product-tooling G4 approval or product publication.",
    "The RTX 5090 ships the exact checked first-build server bab3fd77 under the founder-approved 5090-only reproducibility exception. Same-path nvcc linked builds are not bit-identical; deterministic module IDs remain deferred. This exception does not apply to the reproducible native packages.",
    "The unchanged unmodified upstream OMP 18.14.0 client has no appliance commands. Historical host-free review and binary identities carry unchanged; no predecessor platform or documented-route acceptance qualifies this product candidate.",
    "RTX 5090 retains profile qwen38-5090-v0.13.0, semantic configuration 751d22dc, 131072 context, 146368 automatic BF16 KV tokens, DFlash2 K7, two active requests plus two extra device-state slots and 180-second pending timeout. Fit-dependent C2 is not constant-batch-two or a fairness guarantee.",
    "Native profiles use INT8 DFlash2 K7 with Group64 A8 and FP32 head logits off, 131072 context/KV, strict origin authentication and sequential UUID-bound serving on port 18082. RTX 4090 is C1 with 640 MiB admission headroom, two extra slots, 16512696320 shared Host bytes and 30-second pending timeout. RTX 3090 is C2 over one shared 131072-token pool with 768 MiB headroom, two extra slots, 21881405440 shared Host bytes, 180-second pending timeout and a 350 W serving cap. No native vision, RTX 4090 C2 or smaller-host qualification.",
    "Native schema 3 stores use session-checkpoints-v3 under each immutable component instance. Keep predecessor MTP3 roots and model bytes untouched and replay authoritative OMP transcripts; never import MTP3 generations into DFlash2. The container retains /checkpoints-v013; a kept deployment-profile name does not establish cross-binary checkpoint compatibility.",
    "Strict origin authentication requires a checkpoint root and a bearer key at least 32 bytes. Within one API-key principal, prompt_cache_key names a session capability; use unique high-entropy keys and do not share the principal among mutually untrusted clients. MACs prove origin/content, not monotonic freshness.",
    "Checkpointing is best effort. Windows NTFS ntfs-write-through is not POSIX fsync or power-loss equivalence. Finite import/export and victim-validation I/O can delay decode. Disk reclamation alone does not trigger bounded rearm; Engine/admission progress or explicit client retry is still required.",
    "The current N16 fork council is closed by disposition with deferred residuals tracked in alphastorm/ninfer issues #50 through #54. Its approval does not grant product-tooling review, public-route acceptance or publication. Historical dedicated reproduction trackers are not closed by aggregate lane qualification.",
    "Both native powered screens pass the frozen EXP-085 primary bounds, not a zero-leak or universal quality claim: RTX 3090 leak counts 545 to 561, upper ratio 1.0673; RTX 4090 counts 533 to 561, upper ratio 1.0985; margin 1.10. macOS remains preview and Linux client evidence is WSL2-scoped. Multi-GPU inference, simultaneous supported native serving, multi-tenancy and silent cloud fallback remain unsupported.",
    "RTX 4090 speed retains its raw FAIL and the founder waiver on log-024@0: decode ratio 0.933831973 below the 0.95 every-case floor; weighted role108 and all115 ratios pass. The waiver is hash-bound separately and disclosed in the release notes.",
    "RTX 5090 first-request-after-restart TTFT sometimes takes about 0.5 s rather than about 0.24 s in both engines, with beta.4 slow somewhat more often. Two restore-position TTFT misses retain the founder waiver; all other probe oracles and the admission-order concurrency rule remain binding."
  ],
